---
import { version } from "../../../../npm/magistr/package.json";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Workflow from "../components/Workflow.astro";
import ProductEvidence from "../components/ProductEvidence.astro";

const jsonLd = [
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebSite","name":"Magistr","url":"https://magistr.dev"},
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Magistr","softwareVersion":version,"description":"Plan and build a project with Codex or Claude Code, and pick up the work in your next session.","url":"https://magistr.dev","applicationCategory":"DeveloperApplication","operatingSystem":"macOS (Apple Silicon)","downloadUrl":"https://magistr.dev/docs/installation","softwareRequirements":"macOS 15 or later; Rust 1.95 or later; repository access"}
];
---
<Base title="Magistr — Project planning for Codex and Claude Code" description="Research a project, keep a roadmap, and work through it with your coding agent. Saved decisions, progress and checks help the next session continue." jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero section-shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <h1 id="hero-title">Project planning for Codex and Claude Code.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">Ask your agent to investigate an idea, work out what to build, and carry out the plan. Magistr saves the decisions, progress, and checks so you can review the work and continue in another session.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a id="install-btn" class="button button-primary" href="#install">Set up Magistr</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/workflow">Read the project guide</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">v{version} source preview for Apple Silicon macOS. Repository access required.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="evidence" class="section-shell section-block evidence-section" aria-labelledby="evidence-title" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="evidence-title">The work is there when you come back.</h2>
        <p>These sessions show an agent reading a saved contact-list fix. The desktop capture shows a separate conversation about the same problem.</p>
      </div>
      <ProductEvidence />
    </section>

    <section id="workflow" class="section-shell section-block" aria-labelledby="workflow-title" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="workflow-title">How the contact-list fix was saved</h2>
        <p>The Python function kept names made only of spaces. Follow the recorded task from the failing test to a fresh session reading the result.</p>
      </div>
      <Workflow />
    </section>

    <section id="product" class="section-shell section-block product-section" aria-labelledby="product-title" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="product-title">What to ask your agent</h2>
        <p>Use Magistr for a direct fix, a project review, or a longer run through a roadmap. You can change the plan as you learn more.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="product-details">
        <article><h3>“Look into this before we build it.”</h3><p>Ask the agent to read the code, research the options, and explain its recommendation. Save the findings with the project so later decisions can use them.</p></article>
        <article><h3>“What’s left, and what matters most?”</h3><p>Review the roadmap against the actual code. Reorder the work, split items that are too large, and drop ideas that no longer fit.</p></article>
        <article><h3>“Work through the next five items.”</h3><p>Choose an area and a limit. Have the agent finish, check, and commit each item before continuing. Use <code>magistr next</code> for one item or <code>magistr next-loop</code> for a run with fresh sessions.</p></article>
        <article><h3>“Show me what changed.”</h3><p>Read the diff and try the feature. For an interface, inspect the screens at the sizes you use. Give the agent feedback and have it finish the corrections before moving on.</p></article>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs/workflow">Working on a project with Magistr</a>
    </section>

    <section id="install" class="section-shell section-block install-section" aria-labelledby="install-title" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="install-grid">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="install-title">Set up Magistr</h2>
          <p>Magistr v{version} is a source preview for Apple Silicon macOS. Registry packages are not published yet. You’ll need repository access to build it.</p>
          <p>Requires macOS 15 or later, Rust 1.95 or later, and your own agent account.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/installation">Installation and troubleshooting</a>
        </div>
        <div class="code-panel">
          <div class="code-label"><span>Install from source</span><button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy="source-install" hidden>Copy commands</button></div>
          <pre id="source-install"><code>git clone https://github.com/AlrikOlson/magistr.git
cd magistr
cargo install --locked --path crates/magistr-cli
magistr --version</code></pre>
          <p class="copy-status" data-copy-status role="status"></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ol class="setup-steps">
        <li><h3>Connect your agent</h3><p>Run <code>magistr init .</code> in your project. Choose the agents you want to connect.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Check the setup</h3><p>Run <code>magistr doctor .</code> to check the connection and find anything that needs attention.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Make a plan together</h3><p>Ask your agent to read the project and suggest what to work on. Use <code>$next</code> in Codex or <code>/next</code> in Claude Code when you’re ready to build. Setup does not start implementation.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
<script>
  const copy = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy]");
  if (copy) {
    copy.hidden = false;
    copy.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const text = document.getElementById(copy.dataset.copy!)?.textContent ?? "";
      const status = document.querySelector("[data-copy-status]")!;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
        status.textContent = "Commands copied.";
      } catch {
        status.textContent = "Copy is unavailable. Select the commands above to copy them.";
      }
    });
  }
</script>